      <description>Last words of men and women trapped on high floors of World Trade Center&#39;s twin towers provide haunting chronicle of their final 102 minutes; final words began as calls for help, information, and guidance, and quickly turned into soundings of desperation, anger and love; chronicle is based on scores of phone conversations and e-mail and voice messages; these accounts, along with testimony of handful of people who escaped, provide first sweeping views from floors directly hit by airplanes and above; give human form to advancing destruction across top 19 floors of north tower and top 33 of south, where loss of life was most severe; photos; time line of last 102 minutes at Trade Center (L)</description>
